{"name":"Hydrology","hex":"#89acac","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"hydrology","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The science of the properties, distribution, and effects of water on a planet's surface, in the soil and underlying rocks, and in the atmosphere.","The properties, distribution, and flows of water in a specific locale; the hydrological characteristics of a particular place or region."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hydrology"}],"entries":[{"title":"Hydrology","blocks":[{"text":"Hydrology is the scientific study of the movement, distribution, and management of water on Earth and other planets, including the water cycle, water resources, and drainage basin sustainability. A practitioner of hydrology is called a hydrologist. Hydrologists are scientists studying earth or environmental science, civil or environmental engineering, and physical geography. Using various analytical methods and scientific techniques, they collect and analyze data to help solve water related problems such as environmental preservation, natural disasters, and water management."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/da/Rain_over_Beinn_Eich%2C_Luss_Hills%2C_Scotland.jpg/330px-Rain_over_Beinn_Eich%2C_Luss_Hills%2C_Scotland.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hydrology","wikidata":"Q42250"},{"title":"Hydrology (album)","blocks":[{"text":"Hydrology is the second album by Recoil, released January 25, 1988. It was Alan Wilder's second Recoil release. The CD and cassette version included the first release, 1 + 2."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/2/2a/Recoil_-_Hydrology.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hydrology_(album)","wikidata":"Q1947314"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/61/Caesarea_mari